# Supabase Integration Guidelines

## Client Configuration
The application uses two Supabase clients:

1. Regular Client ([src/integrations/supabase/client.ts](mdc:src/integrations/supabase/client.ts)):
   - Uses anon key for public operations
   - Handles user authentication
   - Used for regular database operations

2. Admin Client ([src/integrations/supabase/admin.ts](mdc:src/integrations/supabase/admin.ts)):
   - Uses service role key for privileged operations
   - Required for admin-only functionality
   - Must be used server-side or in protected admin routes only

## Database Types
- Database types are defined in [src/integrations/supabase/types.ts](mdc:src/integrations/supabase/types.ts)
- Always use these types when interacting with Supabase
- Update types when database schema changes

## Authentication
- Authentication state is managed through [src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx](mdc:src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx)
- Admin role checks are performed using the profile's role field
- Session management includes automatic token refresh

## Best Practices
- Never use admin client for regular user operations
- Always handle Supabase errors appropriately
- Use RLS policies for data access control
- Keep service role key secure and never expose it client-side

